  "callout_language": "Jordanian Arabic military radio with British- and US-style procedure; English terms common in special forces ('contact', 'move', 'cover').",
  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "A small, professional, well-regarded army trained to British and US standards, organised around border defence of long desert frontiers with Syria and Iraq, counter-terrorism and internal security. The King Abdullah II Special Operations Training Center and the Quick Reaction Force are regional training hubs, and Jordanian special forces have long partnered with US and UK units. In 2024-2026 Jordan has shot down Iranian missiles and drones crossing its airspace (including attacks on Azraq air base in 2026), fought heavily armed drug- and arms-smuggling gangs on the Syrian border (now in cooperation with the new Syrian government) and air-dropped aid into Gaza. It banned the Muslim Brotherhood in April 2025.",
    "squad_size": 8,
    "fireteam": "British-style section of 8 in two fireteams with a Minimi and a grenadier, mounted in M113s, Marders or MRAPs; special forces in 4-man patrols. In game: 8 men in battle-buddy pairs.",
    "tactics": [
      "Border berms, towers and fast mobile patrols with rules of engagement that allow firing on armed smugglers",
      "Quick reaction forces with MRAPs and helicopters responding to border incursions",
      "Special forces raids against ISIS cells, often with partner forces",
      "Air defence and drone interception (Jordanian F-16s, counter-drone systems)",
      "Disciplined, methodical infantry movement with good fire control"
    ],
